initial:
Use case: identity-preserve.
Asset type: additional full-body animation sprite sheet for an existing 2D fighting game.
Input image 1 is the exact approved Adriano strike atlas, the primary identity/costume/style/technique reference. Input image 2 is the approved base atlas, the guard and body-proportions reference.
Create a NEW transparent 4-column by 4-row sprite sheet, exactly 16 separate full-body drawings, generous blank space between cells, no text or cell lines. All face toward screen right in the same 3/4 side view as the references. It is ONE man at sixteen moments, not sixteen variants. Preserve his recognisable face, long dark beard, dark swept-back hair with side grey, stocky adult build, white short-sleeve ringer T-shirt with dark collar and sleeve trim, baggy charcoal trousers, black sneakers with white soles and laces. Same painted arcade illustration, black contour, shading and detail density as reference. Fixed camera, fixed character scale, fixed head size, feet on a common baseline within each cell. Do not make him taller/slimmer/more muscular or redesign his face. No weapons, powers, sparks, shadows, ground, ghosts, motion trails, clothing changes, background.
The first TWO rows together are EIGHT chronological drawings of ONE grounded medium straight punch toward the right, from guard through punch to guard:
0 exact relaxed fighting guard based on base reference first frame;
1 small shoulder/hip load, front fist just drawing in, rear hand guards jaw, feet stable;
2 elbow chambered by ribs, rear heel beginning to pivot, shoulder rotating toward right;
3 fist travels forward HALF extended at upper chest height with torso rotation, rear hand guards face;
4 FULL straight punch, fist at opponent chest height, shoulders turn, same technique as strike atlas frame3 (first row last cell), no overreach;
5 fist halfway retracting, shoulders returning, wrist straight, distinct from frame3;
6 fist close to guard with weight settling back onto planted feet;
7 return to the EXACT SAME relaxed guard as frame0.
The last TWO rows together are EIGHT chronological drawings of ONE grounded medium front kick:
8 same relaxed fighting guard;
9 weight shifts onto rear support leg, front heel lifts, hands protect jaw;
10 front knee lifts in front of waist, folded lower leg, balanced support ankle;
11 knee extends halfway, kicking shoe moving toward right at opponent upper torso height, torso modestly leans back;
12 fully extended front kick facing right matching strike reference frame9 (third row second cell), support foot planted;
13 lower leg retracts to chamber with knee still raised, distinct recovery drawing, hands still guarding;
14 kicking leg descends, toe near ground, body returns upright;
15 same relaxed guard as frame8.
Draw genuine continuous whole-body animation with subtle connected torso, pelvis, shoulder and limb changes. Keep the head volume and body mass consistent between all cells. Separate figures cleanly with ample transparent padding; each entire head, hand, toe and support shoe must fit in its own cell. No overlaps or clipped extremities. True alpha transparency. This is production animation material, not a poster or character-design sheet.
